{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1557","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Ezzat and Two Subsequences"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ezzat has an array of $$$n$$$ integers "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"(maybe negative)"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". He wants to split it into two "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"non-empty"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" subsequences $$$a$$$ and $$$b$$$, such that every element from the array belongs to exactly one subsequence, and the value of $$$f(a) + f(b)$$$ is the maximum possible value, where $$$f(x)$$$ is the average of the subsequence $$$x$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A sequence $$$x$$$ is a subsequence of a sequence $$$y$$$ if $$$x$$$ can be obtained from $$$y$$$ by deletion of several (possibly, zero or all) elements."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The average of a subsequence is the sum of the numbers of this subsequence divided by the size of the subsequence."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, the average of $$$[1,5,6]$$$ is $$$(1+5+6)/3 = 12/3 = 4$$$, so $$$f([1,5,6]) = 4$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^3$$$)— the number of test cases. Each test case consists of two lines."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 10^5$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ ($$$-10^9 \\le a_i \\le 10^9$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$3\\cdot10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print a single value — the maximum value that Ezzat can achieve."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your answer is considered correct if its absolute or relative error does not exceed $$$10^{-6}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Formally, let your answer be $$$a$$$, and the jury's answer be $$$b$$$. Your answer is accepted if and only if $$$\\frac{|a - b|}{\\max{(1, |b|)}} \\le 10^{-6}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n3\n3 1 2\n3\n-7 -6 -6\n3\n2 2 2\n4\n17 3 5 -3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4.500000000\n-12.500000000\n4.000000000\n18.666666667\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, the array is $$$[3, 1, 2]$$$. These are all the possible ways to split this array: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a = [3]$$$, $$$b = [1,2]$$$, so the value of $$$f(a) + f(b) = 3 + 1.5 = 4.5$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a = [3,1]$$$, $$$b = [2]$$$, so the value of $$$f(a) + f(b) = 2 + 2 = 4$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a = [3,2]$$$, $$$b = [1]$$$, so the value of $$$f(a) + f(b) = 2.5 + 1 = 3.5$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" Therefore, the maximum possible value $$$4.5$$$."},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, the array is $$$[-7, -6, -6]$$$. These are all the possible ways to split this array: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a = [-7]$$$, $$$b = [-6,-6]$$$, so the value of $$$f(a) + f(b) = (-7) + (-6) = -13$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a = [-7,-6]$$$, $$$b = [-6]$$$, so the value of $$$f(a) + f(b) = (-6.5) + (-6) = -12.5$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" Therefore, the maximum possible value $$$-12.5$$$."}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"1557A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1557/problem/A"}